  "schema:name": "10m Annual Land Use Land Cover (9-class)",
  "schema:description": "Time series of annual global maps of land use and land cover (LULC). It currently has data from 2017-2024. The maps are derived from ESA Sentinel-2 imagery at 10m resolution. Each map is a composite of LULC predictions for 9 classes throughout the year in order to generate a representative snapshot of each year. This dataset was generated by [Impact Observatory](http://impactobservatory.com/), who used billions of human-labeled pixels (curated by the National Geographic Society) to train a deep learning model for land classification. The global map was produced by applying this model to the Sentinel-2 annual scene collections on the Planetary Computer. Each of the maps has an assessed average accuracy of over 75%. All years are available under a Creative Commons BY-4.0.",
